# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/pools/statuses.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event hungry_leftovers
# en: The Refectory's Leftovers
title [dbc5bf] = 膳堂的剩饭
# en: {The refectory is closing, and the kitchens are scraping the pots. A cook sees you hovering in the doorway and holds up a ladle, eyebrows raised.|The same cook, the same ladle. She doesn't ask any more; she just raises her eyebrows.|You know the kitchens' closing time to the minute now.} {A prefect is still at the end table, finishing an essay.|Two first-years are sweeping, and watching.}
text [50fc74] = {膳堂快关门了，厨房在刮锅底。一个厨娘看见你在门口徘徊，举起汤勺，扬了扬眉毛。|还是那个厨娘，还是那把汤勺。她不再问了，只扬扬眉毛。|如今你对厨房关门的时间精确到分钟。}{尽头的桌子边还坐着一个级长，在赶论文。|两个一年级生在扫地，一边扫一边看。}
# en: A refectory kitchen door at closing time, a cook scraping the last of a stew into a bowl for a student waiting in the doorway.
scene [8b6728] = 关门时分膳堂的厨房门口，厨娘把最后一点炖菜刮进碗里，递给等在门边的学生。
# en: Take the bowl
opt.left.label [629c3f] = 接过那碗
# en: {It's the burnt bit at the bottom of the stew and it is the best thing you've ever eaten. The prefect looks up from her essay and remembers your face.|The cook fills the bowl to the brim. The first-years see, and by breakfast half your year knows why.}
opt.left.say.1 [f366f1] = {是炖菜锅底烧焦的那层，却是你吃过最好吃的东西。级长从论文上抬起头，记住了你的脸。|厨娘把碗盛得满满的。一年级生们看见了，到早饭时，你们年级一半人都知道为什么。}
# en: Shake your head and leave
opt.right.label [d3d37c] = 摇摇头走开
# en: {"Not hungry," you say, to nobody in particular, and go upstairs on an empty stomach that disagrees.|You walk out with your pride and nothing else. Your stomach complains all night.}
opt.right.say.1 [c308da] = {“不饿，”你对着空气说，空着肚子上了楼，肚子不同意。|你带着自尊离开，别的什么也没带。你的肚子抱怨了一整夜。}

@event hungry_pocketed_rolls
# en: Rolls for Later
title [e2a96a] = 留着以后吃的面包
# en: {The refectory's bread rolls are piled high. Board-payers only, says the sign; it doesn't say how many.|The rolls again, and the sign again, and your empty pockets.|Another meal. You've got good at looking as if you've paid.} {The prefect on duty is reading a letter.|The prefect on duty is looking straight at the bread.}
text [734a8a] = {食堂的面包卷堆得高高的。告示写着只供交了食宿费的人；没写能拿几个。|又是面包卷，又是那块告示，又是你空空的口袋。|又一顿饭。你已经很会装作交过钱的样子了。}{值班的级长在读信。|值班的级长正盯着面包。}
# en: A breakfast table heaped with bread rolls, a student's hand hovering near a pocket while a prefect patrols the aisle.
scene [5e16e9] = 堆满面包卷的早餐桌，一个学生的手在口袋边犹豫，一个级长在过道里巡视。
# en: Pocket a few for later
opt.left.label [daa943] = 揣几个留着
# en: {Three rolls in your robe, still warm. They last a day, and so does the guilt.|You fill your pockets and walk out at an even pace, crumbs and all.|Two rolls and an apple. Nobody stops you. You eat them on the stairs, a little ashamed.}
opt.left.say.1 [b89f46] = {三个面包卷揣进袍子里，还是热的。它们撑了一整天，内疚也是。|你塞满口袋，不紧不慢地走出去，连面包屑一起。|两个面包卷加一个苹果。没人拦你。你坐在楼梯上吃完，有点羞愧。}
# en: Eat what's on your plate
opt.right.label [7782d7] = 只吃盘里的
# en: {One roll, eaten slowly, and nothing taken that isn't yours. By the next meal you're light-headed and honest.|You eat what you're given, and the hunger keeps you company for hours.}
opt.right.say.1 [b18681] = {一个面包卷，慢慢吃，不拿不属于你的东西。到下一顿饭时你头晕眼花，但问心无愧。|给什么吃什么，饥饿陪了你好几个钟头。}

@event hungry_maud_soup
# en: Soup at the Cottage
title [b46ed5] = 小屋里的汤
# en: {Old Maud catches you on the path by her cottage. "You've a hungry look, dearie. Come and eat." She has a pot on already, as if she knew.|Maud's pot is on again. She doesn't ask, and you don't explain.} {The soup is leek and something she won't name.|A bee sits on the windowsill, waiting for its share.}
text [019fd3] = {老莫德在她小屋旁的小路上拦住你。“你一脸饿相，亲爱的。进来吃点。”她的锅已经炖上了，好像早就知道。|莫德的锅又炖上了。她不问，你也不解释。}{汤里有韭葱，还有一样她不肯说的东西。|窗台上落着一只蜜蜂，等着分一份。}
# en: A crooked cottage kitchen full of hanging herbs, an old woman ladling soup from a black pot into a chipped bowl.
scene [65b863] = 歪歪扭扭的小屋厨房里挂满草药，一位老妇人从黑锅里舀汤倒进一只缺口的碗。
# en: Stay for soup and a story
opt.left.label [16b691] = 留下喝汤听故事
# en: {Two bowls, bread, and a sad story about her sister told like a recipe. Your reading waits until morning, and it'll be late.|She talks about the winter the lake froze twice while you eat. The essay you meant to write tonight stays unwritten.}
opt.left.say.1 [309b82] = {两碗汤、面包，还有一个关于她姐姐的伤心故事，讲得像菜谱一样。你的阅读只好等到明早，肯定要迟交了。|你吃饭时，她讲起湖结了两次冰的那个冬天。你本打算今晚写的论文，一个字也没写。}
# en: Take a jar back to your room
opt.right.label [6ec9c2] = 带一罐回房间
# en: {She fills a jar and wraps it in a cloth. "Bring the jar back," she says. "That's the price." You eat at your desk, studying.|You carry the warm jar up the hill and eat it over your books. Maud waves from the door, a little disappointed.}
opt.right.say.1 [f489b9] = {她装了一罐，用布包好。“罐子要还回来，”她说，“这就是价钱。”你坐在书桌前边吃边学。|你捧着温热的罐子走上山，对着书本吃完。莫德在门口挥手，有点失望。}

@event detention_cauldrons
# en: Cauldron Duty
title [f28745] = 刷坩埚
# en: {Detention, and a row of crusted cauldrons and a prefect by the door with a book.|Detention again. The cauldrons are the same; the crust is worse.|You know these cauldrons by name now. One of them, you suspect, knows you.} {Something in the third one is still bubbling.|The prefect is pretending not to be bored.}
text [135d89] = {禁闭，一排结满污垢的坩埚，门口一个拿着书的级长。|又是禁闭。坩埚还是那些，污垢更厚了。|这些坩埚你都叫得出名字了。你怀疑其中一只也认得你。}{第三只里还有东西在冒泡。|级长在假装不无聊。}
# en: A dim potions storeroom, a student up to the elbows in a crusted cauldron while a prefect reads by a lamp at the door.
scene [942c95] = 昏暗的魔药储藏室，一个学生胳膊伸进结垢的坩埚里直到手肘，门边一个级长借着灯光看书。
# en: Scrub them properly
opt.left.label [1ea45b] = 好好刷干净
# en: {You scrub until your knuckles are raw, and learn which residues bite back and which only sulk.|By the last cauldron you can tell a week-old draught from a month-old one by the smell alone. Your hands sting for days.}
opt.left.say.1 [b1bfb9] = {你刷到指节发红，学会了哪些残渣会反咬一口，哪些只会闹脾气。|刷到最后一只时，你光凭气味就能分辨放了一周和放了一个月的药剂。你的手刺痛了好几天。}
# en: Talk your way to an early night
opt.right.label [358ac0] = 说服级长早点放人
# en: {You talk about the prefect's book until the prefect is talking about it too, and at nine they wave you off. "Same time next week. Possibly."|You find out you're both from the same county. The cauldrons can wait for someone less charming.}
opt.right.say.1 [f8daa1] = {你跟级长聊起他手里那本书，聊到他自己也聊开了，九点就挥手放你走。“下周同一时间。大概吧。”|你们发现彼此是同乡。坩埚可以留给不那么讨人喜欢的人。}
# en: {"Nice try," says the prefect, and hands you the worst cauldron in the row.|The prefect hears you out, then points at the third cauldron, the bubbling one. "For the speech."}
opt.right.say.2 [e81c64] = {“想得美，”级长说，把那一排里最糟的坩埚递给了你。|级长听你说完，指了指第三口坩埚，还在冒泡的那口。“奖励你的演讲。”}

@event detention_lines
# en: Lines, With Company
title [e410cf] = 有人作伴的罚抄
# en: Detention means lines, a hundred of them, and {other} is at the next desk doing the same. {~The sentence is "I will not bring livestock into the library."|The sentence is "Curfew is not a suggestion."|The sentence is "Stairs are for walking."} An enchanted quill at the front of the room writes down everything anyone says.
text [10752a] = 禁闭就是罚抄，一百遍，{other}就在隔壁桌抄同样的东西。{~句子是“我不会把牲口带进图书馆。”|句子是“宵禁不是建议。”|句子是“楼梯是用来走的。”}教室前面有一支施了魔法的羽毛笔，会把任何人说的每句话都记下来。
# en: An empty classroom at dusk, two students at separate desks writing the same sentence over and over, a quill scratching on its own at the front.
scene [e7f96f] = 黄昏时空荡荡的教室，两个学生坐在不同的桌前一遍遍抄同一句话，前面一支羽毛笔自己沙沙地写着。
# en: Do your homework under the desk
opt.left.label [9b4823] = 在桌子底下写作业
# en: {~A hundred lines and an evening's revision for every course. The quill at the front records nothing but scratching.|You alternate a line and a page of notes. Nobody checks. Your whole week's reading is the better for it.}
opt.left.say.1 [29d2a6] = {~一百遍罚抄，外加把每门课都复习了一晚上。前面的羽毛笔除了沙沙声什么也没记下。|你抄一行，看一页笔记，交替进行。没人检查。你这一整周的功课都因此更扎实了。}
# en: {~The prefect lifts your lines, finds your notes underneath and confiscates them until the end of term.|Your notes fall on the floor at exactly the wrong moment. The prefect keeps them, and makes you start the lines again.}
opt.left.say.2 [18ef3a] = {~级长掀起你的罚抄纸，发现底下的笔记，一直没收到学期结束。|你的笔记在最不该掉的时候掉到了地上。级长收走了它们，还让你从头再抄。}
# en: Talk to {other}
opt.right.label [730ff0] = 和{other}聊天
# en: {~By the fortieth line you know why {other} is here, and it's a better story than yours. The quill at the front writes it all down, word for word.|You compare crimes. {other} laughs so hard the quill at the front writes "LAUGHTER" in capitals.}
opt.right.say.1 [1e9a62] = {~抄到第四十遍时，你已经知道{other}为什么在这儿了，比你的故事精彩。前面的羽毛笔一字不差地全记了下来。|你们比较各自的罪行。{other}笑得太厉害，前面的羽毛笔用大写写下了“笑声”。}

@event probation_advisor
# en: A Word With Your Advisor
title [98682b] = 和导师谈谈
# en: {A summons to your advisor's office. Your marks lie on the desk between you, upside down for you, right way up for them.|Your advisor again, and the same marks, a little better or a little worse.} "Two terms under the line and the Disciplinary Board sits," they say. "Shall we make sure it doesn't?"
text [00903e] = {你被叫到导师办公室。你的成绩单摆在你们中间的桌上，对你是倒着的，对他们是正着的。|又是导师，又是那份成绩，好了一点或者差了一点。}“连续两个学期低于及格线，纪律委员会就要开会了，”他们说，“我们一起确保这不会发生，好吗？”
# en: A cluttered faculty office with a ticking clock, an advisor and a student either side of a desk with a marks list between them.
scene [edee64] = 杂乱的教职员办公室里时钟滴答作响，导师和学生隔着书桌坐着，中间放着成绩单。
# en: Make a study plan together
opt.left.label [c5684e] = 一起订个学习计划
# en: {An hour later you have a timetable that colours every evening grey, and you start on the first evening of it that night. It is a very good timetable. You hate it.|The plan has a column for sleep, and it is narrow. You work through the first week of it with your advisor checking in.}
opt.left.say.1 [e6ba58] = {一小时后，你得到一张把每个晚上都涂成灰色的时间表，当晚就照着它开始了第一晚。这是一张非常好的时间表。你恨它。|计划里有一栏是睡觉，那一栏很窄。你按它熬过了第一周，导师时不时过问一下。}
# en: Talk about what's going wrong
opt.right.label [d074c1] = 聊聊出了什么问题
# en: {You say aloud the thing you hadn't said to anyone. Your advisor listens and makes no plan at all. You leave lighter, and no better prepared.|It turns out your advisor failed a year, once. You talk about that instead of your marks.}
opt.right.say.1 [0f21a6] = {你把从没对人说过的话说出了口。导师听着，一点计划也没订。你离开时轻松了些，准备却一点没多。|原来你的导师也曾留过一级。你们聊的是这个，而不是你的成绩。}

@event probation_letter
# en: The Warning Letter
title [a7ab28] = 警告信
# en: A letter from the registrar, in the stiff envelope everyone dreads: Academic Probation, your name spelled correctly for once, and a line about "consequences" underlined twice. A copy, it says, has gone to your family.
text [29a24a] = 教务处来信，装在人人害怕的那种硬邦邦的信封里：学业察看，你的名字难得拼对了，“后果”一词下面画了两道线。信上说，副本已寄给你的家人。
# en: A stiff envelope with the academy's seal lying open on a desk, a student holding the letter at arm's length.
scene [f197c9] = 书桌上一个盖着学院火漆的硬信封已经拆开，一个学生把信拿得远远的。
# en: Pin it above your desk
opt.left.label [94c02c] = 钉在书桌上方
# en: The letter glares at you every time you look up. It works, in the way a headache works: you study, and you don't enjoy a minute of it.
opt.left.say.1 [2e8283] = 你每次抬头，那封信都瞪着你。它管用，就像头疼管用一样：你学了，但没有一分钟是享受的。
# en: Put it in a drawer
opt.right.label [73100a] = 放进抽屉
# en: Out of sight, mostly out of mind. Mostly. Some nights you open the drawer, look at it and close the drawer again.
opt.right.say.1 [9a09b4] = 眼不见，心大致不烦。大致。有些晚上你拉开抽屉，看它一眼，又关上。

@event sick_in_the_infirmary
# en: A Bed by the Window
title [d71099] = 窗边的病床
# en: {Lake fever. Your nose glows faintly blue, and Sister Amaranth says "Bed," in the voice that means it.|The fever again, and the same bed by the window.} {Lectures are going on without you.|Someone has left a stack of notes on the chair.}
text [3abe07] = {湖热病。你的鼻尖泛着淡蓝的光，阿玛兰斯修女说了声“躺下”，用的是不容商量的语气。|又发烧了，还是窗边那张床。}{课在没有你的情况下照常进行。|有人在椅子上留了一沓笔记。}
# en: A row of white infirmary beds, a student wrapped in blankets with a faintly glowing blue nose and a steaming mug beside them.
scene [0cb8c2] = 一排白色的医务室病床，一个学生裹着毯子，鼻尖发着淡淡的蓝光，身边放着一杯冒热气的饮品。
# en: Stay in bed all week
opt.left.label [1adbad] = 卧床一整周
# en: {You sleep, drink something bitter and sleep again. When you go back, the class is two chapters ahead.|A week of blankets and broth. You feel much better and know much less.}
opt.left.say.1 [7b6e03] = {你睡觉，喝点苦东西，再睡。等你回去，班上已经讲到两章以后了。|一周的毯子和肉汤。你感觉好多了，知道的却少多了。}
# en: Go to lectures in a scarf
opt.right.label [f539a4] = 围着围巾去上课
# en: {You sniffle through Arcana in three scarves. The notes are good; the coughing fit in the middle is not.|You make every lecture, and every lecture makes you worse. Sister Amaranth sees you on the stairs and says nothing, very loudly.}
opt.right.say.1 [fa9f22] = {你围着三条围巾吸着鼻子上完了奥术课。笔记记得很好，中途那阵咳嗽就不好了。|每节课你都去了，每节课都让你病得更重。阿玛兰斯修女在楼梯上看见你，什么也没说，说得很大声。}

@event injured_on_the_stairs
# en: The Moving Stairs, Limping
title [442cc2] = 瘸着腿走会动的楼梯
# en: {Your ankle is bandaged and the stairs are moving, as stairs here do. The lecture is three landings up and starts in five minutes.|The stairs again, the ankle again. The lecture, as ever, is at the top.}
text [c197eb] = {你的脚踝缠着绷带，而楼梯在动，这里的楼梯就是这样。课在三层楼梯之上，五分钟后开始。|又是楼梯，又是脚踝。课照旧在最上面。}
# en: A grand staircase swinging slowly between landings, a student with a bandaged ankle clinging to the banister as it moves.
scene [6c9dff] = 一道宏伟的楼梯在两个平台之间缓缓摆动，一个脚踝缠着绷带的学生紧抓着移动的扶手。
# en: Take the long way, slowly
opt.left.label [c434dc] = 绕远路，慢慢走
# en: {You limp round by the back corridor and arrive as everyone is packing up. The ankle thanks you; your notes don't.|Slow, careful and very late. The ankle mends a little faster for it.}
opt.left.say.1 [27a6aa] = {你一瘸一拐地绕过后走廊，到的时候大家正在收拾东西。脚踝谢谢你；你的笔记不谢。|慢、小心，迟到很久。脚踝因此好得快了一点。}
# en: Hop the gap as it swings
opt.right.label [eee215] = 趁它摆过来时跳过去
# en: {You time it perfectly and land on one foot. Somebody on the landing applauds.|One hop, one wobble, one bow. You're on time and briefly famous.}
opt.right.say.1 [25eaae] = {你把握好时机，单脚落地。平台上有人鼓掌。|一跳，一晃，一鞠躬。你准时到了，还短暂地出了名。}
# en: {You land on the wrong foot, the bad one. The stairs swing on without you, and you sit on the step for a while.|The gap is wider than it looked. You arrive on time and limping twice as badly.}
opt.right.say.2 [87c7cb] = {你落在了错的那只脚上，伤的那只。楼梯丢下你摆走了，你在台阶上坐了好一会儿。|缝隙比看上去宽。你准时到了，瘸得比原来厉害一倍。}

@event purse_and_the_board
# en: A Light Purse
title [a59033] = 钱袋空空
# en: {You tip out your purse on the bed. Three coins and a button.|The purse again. The button is still there; the coins are fewer.} Board is due at the start of every month. {On the way to breakfast you passed the Job Board in the entrance hall, and someone was taking down a notice.|Someone in your year says the Newt is hiring again.|There's a hardship notice by the bursar's door, someone says, and professors who pay for errands.}
text [e40acb] = {你把钱袋倒在床上。三枚硬币，一颗纽扣。|又是这个钱袋。纽扣还在，硬币更少了。}每个月初都要交食宿费。{去吃早饭的路上，你经过门厅的招工告示板，有人正在揭下一张告示。|你们年级有人说，蝾螈酒馆又在招人了。|有人说，财务官门边贴着困难补助的告示，还有教授会花钱请人跑腿。}
# en: A student emptying a coin purse on a dormitory bed, three coins and a button rolling out across the blanket.
scene [edb439] = 一个学生把钱袋倒在宿舍床上，三枚硬币和一颗纽扣滚过毯子。
# en: Sell your second-best cloak
opt.left.label [da0dc9] = 卖掉你第二好的斗篷
# en: {A second-hand stall in the village gives you a fair price and an unfair look. The castle is draughty without it.|You sell the cloak. It was your grandmother's. You're nearly sure she'd understand.}
opt.left.say.1 [ddbe7d] = {山下小镇的二手摊给了你一个公道的价钱，和一个不太公道的眼神。没了它，城堡里冷飕飕的。|你卖掉了斗篷。那是你祖母的。你几乎可以肯定她会理解。}
# en: Look at the Job Board later
opt.right.label [e5acc5] = 回头去看看招工告示板
# en: {You make a note. The Job Board, entrance hall, morning to evening. One job at a time, paid by the shift.|You'll go and read the notices. Probably. Board is due either way.}
opt.right.say.1 [5d0e71] = {你记下：招工告示板，门厅，早上到傍晚。一次一份工，按班次付钱。|你会去看看那些告示的。大概吧。反正食宿费总是要交的。}

@event ember_on_the_essay
# en: A Fox on the Essay
title [342c5e] = 论文上的狐狸
# en: {Ember has chosen your week's coursework to sleep on, and her tail is smouldering, as it does when she dreams.|Ember is asleep on your notes again. The corner of every page is already brown.|Ember has a new favourite sleeping place, and all of it is due on Monday.}
text [365726] = {余烬选中你这一周的功课当床，尾巴冒着烟，她做梦时总是这样。|余烬又在你的笔记上睡着了。每一页的纸角都已经焦黄。|余烬有了新的心头好睡觉地点，而且这些全都周一要交。}
# en: A fox-spirit curled asleep on a student's half-written essay, her tail smouldering gently at one corner of the page.
scene [0a42c9] = 一只狐灵蜷在学生写了一半的论文上睡觉，尾巴在纸角轻轻冒烟。
# en: Rescue the essay
opt.left.label [e5bb3c] = 抢救论文
# en: {You slide the pile out from under her. She opens one eye, says something rude in fox and sulks under the bed until supper.|You rescue the pages and lose a fox: she spends the evening on your pillow with her back to you.}
opt.left.say.1 [76c85d] = {你把那摞纸从她身下抽出来。她睁开一只眼，用狐狸语说了句难听的话，然后躲到床底下生闷气，一直到晚饭。|你救下了那几页纸，却失去了一只狐狸：她整晚背对着你趴在你的枕头上。}
# en: Let her sleep and write around her
opt.right.label [775316] = 让她睡，绕着她写
# en: {You write the conclusion in the margin, round a sleeping fox. Your essays come back scorched at one corner and marked down for it.|She's warm, she's purring in her own way, and your notes have a hole in them now. It's worth it.}
opt.right.say.1 [f556aa] = {你绕着一只熟睡的狐狸，把结论写在了页边。论文发回来时一角烧焦了，还因此被扣了分。|她暖暖的，以她自己的方式打着呼噜，你的笔记现在多了个洞。值得。}

@event ember_night_hunt
# en: Ember Goes Hunting
title [093af9] = 余烬去打猎
# en: {Ember tugs at your blanket. Then at your sleeve. Then at your ear. She wants you to come.|Ember is at the door again, tail glowing, waiting.} {Somewhere below, something is scratching.|The corridors are cold and very quiet.}
text [184d85] = {余烬拽你的毯子。然后拽你的袖子。然后拽你的耳朵。她想让你跟着来。|余烬又守在门口，尾巴发着光，等着。}{楼下某处，有什么东西在抓挠。|走廊又冷又静。}
# en: A dark castle corridor lit only by the glow of a fox's tail, a student in a nightgown following at a distance.
scene [050b20] = 只有狐狸尾巴的微光照亮的昏暗城堡走廊，一个穿睡袍的学生远远跟在后面。
# en: Follow her through the castle
opt.left.label [8c04fb] = 跟着她穿过城堡
# en: {She leads you down three staircases to a loose stone, and sits by it, very pleased. Behind it, nothing but a draught. You're back at dawn, frozen.|A mouse, two corridors and a door you'd never noticed. You get back to bed cold and much better at walking quietly.}
opt.left.say.1 [cc981e] = {她领你走下三段楼梯，来到一块松动的石头前，坐在旁边，得意极了。石头后面：除了一股穿堂风什么也没有。你天亮才回去，冻得透透的。|一只老鼠，两条走廊，一扇你从没注意过的门。你回到床上时浑身冰凉，走路却轻了许多。}
# en: Pull the blanket over your head
opt.right.label [352adf] = 把毯子蒙过头
# en: {You sleep. Ember goes alone and comes back at dawn smelling of the kitchens, enormously smug.|She sighs at you, a fox's sigh, and goes without you. You sleep like a stone.}
opt.right.say.1 [55c90a] = {你睡了。余烬独自出门，天亮回来时一身厨房的味道，得意得不得了。|她冲你叹了口气，狐狸式的叹气，自己去了。你睡得像块石头。}

@event ember_and_the_sandwich
# en: The Prefect's Sandwich
title [4bfec6] = 级长的三明治
# en: Ember trots through the refectory with a prefect's sandwich in her jaws, past forty witnesses. The prefect looks at the empty plate, then at the fox, then at the room. "Whose," the prefect says, "is that?"
text [3b22cb] = 余烬叼着一个级长的三明治，从四十个目击者面前小跑着穿过膳堂。级长看看空盘子，看看狐狸，又看看满屋子的人。“这是谁的，”级长说，“那只？”
# en: A crowded refectory, a small fire-tailed fox trotting off with a sandwich while a prefect stares at an empty plate.
scene [928f92] = 拥挤的膳堂里，一只火尾小狐狸叼着三明治小跑而去，一个级长瞪着空盘子。
# en: Own up and buy a new one
opt.left.label [66e428] = 认了，再买一个
# en: You raise your hand. The room laughs; you pay for a sandwich at the counter and hand it over. The prefect accepts it with dignity. Ember eats the first one under your chair.
opt.left.say.1 [27502f] = 你举起手。满屋子的人都笑了；你在柜台买了个三明治递过去。级长庄重地收下了。余烬在你椅子底下吃掉了第一个。
# en: Look as puzzled as everyone else
opt.right.label [c5a60c] = 跟大家一样一脸茫然
# en: You look around the room, as baffled as anybody. Ember sits on your foot under the table, chewing. The prefect never finds out, and Ember never lets you forget it.
opt.right.say.1 [cbaa51] = 你环顾四周，和所有人一样困惑。余烬坐在桌下你的脚上嚼着。级长始终没查出来，而余烬始终不让你忘了这件事。

@event owl_six_oclock
# en: "HOMEWORK"
title [a40fe3] = “作业”
# en: {Bedtime. "HOMEWORK," says the clockwork owl, and then, because you haven't moved, "HOMEWORK. DUE. TOMORROW."|"HOMEWORK," says the owl, at bedtime, as ever. This time it's right. A week's exercises are due tomorrow, in every course, and you'd forgotten.|The owl's bedtime hoot has a new word in it: "LATE."}
text [3d755a] = {睡觉时间。“作业，”发条猫头鹰说，见你没动，又说：“作业。明天。要交。”|“作业，”猫头鹰照例在睡前说。这次它说对了。每门课都有一周的练习明天要交，你给忘了。|猫头鹰睡前的报时里多了一个新词：“迟了。”}
# en: A brass clockwork owl on a bedpost at dawn, its amber eyes glowing, a student groaning under a pillow.
scene [d3576f] = 黎明时床柱上站着一只黄铜发条猫头鹰，琥珀色眼睛发着光，一个学生在枕头底下呻吟。
# en: Stay up and write it now
opt.left.label [e04890] = 熬夜马上写
# en: {You write it all by candlelight with your eyes half shut. It's not your best work, but it's in. The owl says "GOOD," which you didn't know it could.|Two hours of frantic quill-work by the last of the candle. You hand it in on time and nod off in the next lecture.}
opt.left.say.1 [ebe88a] = {你半睁着眼在烛光下全部写完。不是你最好的作品，但交上了。猫头鹰说“好”，你都不知道它会说这个。|就着最后一截蜡烛奋笔疾书了两个钟头。你按时交了，下一节课却打起了瞌睡。}
# en: Hand it in late
opt.right.label [6db6d8] = 迟交
# en: {You go to sleep. The owl says "DISAPPOINTED" twice and goes quiet. Your work goes in a day late and is marked accordingly.|You sleep until eight. The owl doesn't speak to you until lunch, and then only to say "LATE."}
opt.right.say.1 [7cf42e] = {你去睡了。猫头鹰说了两遍“失望”，然后不吭声了。你的作业晚交了一天，分数也相应打了折。|你一觉睡到八点。猫头鹰直到午饭都不理你，开口也只说“迟了”。}

@event owl_birthday
# en: "BIRTHDAY"
title [8d676a] = “生日”
# en: "BIRTHDAY," says the owl, flapping in front of your face, and then, louder, "BIRTHDAY." It turns its head toward the window, toward the dormitory where {friend} lives. Mir built it to remember birthdays. You had not.
text [2c9379] = “生日，”猫头鹰扑棱着翅膀在你面前说，然后更大声：“生日。”它把头转向窗外，转向{friend}住的那栋宿舍。米尔造它时就让它记生日。你可没记。
# en: A clockwork owl fluttering in front of a student, its beak open mid-hoot, a calendar on the wall behind.
scene [65c33f] = 一只发条猫头鹰在学生面前扑腾，喙张着正在叫，身后墙上挂着日历。
# en: Buy a proper present
opt.left.label [c20c31] = 买份像样的礼物
# en: You run down to the village before the shops close and come back with something {friend} actually wanted. {They} look{s} at you as if you've always remembered.
opt.left.say.1 [6c6795] = 你赶在商店关门前跑下山，带回一样{friend}真正想要的东西。{They}看着你，好像你一直都记得。
# en: Write a card, quickly
opt.right.label [74c735] = 赶紧写张卡片
# en: A card, a drawing of the owl and "Happy birthday" in your best hand. {friend} pins it up anyway, and asks how you knew.
opt.right.say.1 [5972f0] = 一张卡片，画了那只猫头鹰，用你最好的字写着“生日快乐”。{friend}还是把它钉了起来，问你是怎么知道的。

@event owl_wound_down
# en: The Owl Winds Down
title [cca46b] = 猫头鹰没电了
# en: The clockwork owl has started saying "HOME… WORK…" very slowly, like a music box running down. One wing droops. There is a tiny panel in its chest, and a tinier key, and absolutely no instructions.
text [20f376] = 发条猫头鹰开始很慢很慢地说“作……业……”，像一只快走完的八音盒。一边翅膀耷拉着。它胸口有个小小的盖板，一把更小的钥匙，没有任何说明。
# en: A brass owl slumped on a desk with one wing drooping, a student peering into a small open panel in its chest with a magnifying glass.
scene [c0c42f] = 一只黄铜猫头鹰瘫在桌上，一边翅膀下垂，一个学生拿着放大镜往它胸口打开的小盖板里看。
# en: Take it back to Mir
opt.left.label [e10bd7] = 带回去给米尔
# en: Mir lights up and spends the whole evening inside the owl with tweezers, explaining every spring. You miss your reading entirely. The owl comes back saying "HOMEWORK" faster than ever.
opt.left.say.1 [7214a4] = 米尔眼睛一亮，整个晚上都拿着镊子钻在猫头鹰肚子里，一根根发条地讲解。你的阅读完全泡汤了。猫头鹰回来后说“作业”说得比以前还快。
# en: Fix it yourself
opt.right.label [bf3e8e] = 自己修
# en: A wound spring, a drop of oil and a charm to keep it turning. The owl shakes itself and says "THANK YOU," which it has never said before.
opt.right.say.1 [1c89db] = 上紧一根发条，滴一滴油，再加一道让它转下去的咒语。猫头鹰抖了抖身子，说了声“谢谢”，它以前从没说过。
# en: You fix it. Now it hoots on the half hour instead of the hour, all night, and says "HOMEWORK" in a voice like a kettle.
opt.right.say.2 [ca3ce4] = 你修好了。现在它不是整点报时，而是每半点报一次，整夜都报，说“作业”的声音像烧开的水壶。
